{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/pulls/21312","id":3705108068,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAD-Lgs7c13Zk","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/21312","diff_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/21312.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/21312.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/21312","number":21312,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Refs #28905 -- Declared optional dependencies in pyproject.toml","user":{"login":"darwing1210","id":18296414,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjk2NDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18296414?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210","html_url":"https://github.com/darwing1210","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darwing1210/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"#### Trac ticket number\n\nticket-28905\n\n#### Branch description\n\nDeclares all of Django's optional Python dependencies in `pyproject.toml`, making\nthem installable as pip extras (e.g. `pip install \"django[postgresql,gis]\"`).\nReplaces the `tests/requirements/` directory with PEP 735 dependency groups,\nconsolidating all dependency management into a single file. Adds a new\ndocumentation page covering every optional extra with purpose, version\nrequirements, and install instructions.\n\n**pip extras added** (`[project.optional-dependencies]`)\n\nNew extras: `admindocs`, `colorama`, `geoip`, `gis`, `images`, `jinja2`,\n`mysql`, `oracle`, `postgresql`, `postgresql-pool`, `pylibmc`, `pymemcache`,\n`pywatchman`, `redis`, `selenium`, `test-parallel`, `yaml`. The existing\n`argon2` and `bcrypt` extras are unchanged.\n\n**PEP 735 dependency groups added** (`[dependency-groups]`)\n\nSix groups replace `tests/requirements/*.txt`: `test`, `postgres`, `mysql`,\n`oracle`, and the composed `test-postgres`, `test-mysql`, `test-oracle`. All\nGitHub Actions workflows updated to use `--group` (requires pip 25.1+).\n\n**Notable decisions**\n\n- `postgresql` vs `postgresql-pool`: the base extra installs only `psycopg`\n  for basic connectivity; `postgresql-pool` additionally installs `psycopg-pool`\n  for projects using Django's server-side connection pooling. The\n  `ImproperlyConfigured` error message when pool support is missing now\n  references `django[postgresql-pool]`.\n\n- `psycopg` (no `[binary]`) for user-facing extras, `psycopg[binary]` for CI\n  dependency groups: production Linux users link against system `libpq`; CI\n  runners do not need it.\n\n- `colorama` carries a `sys_platform == 'win32'` marker — it is only useful\n  on Windows and the marker makes that constraint explicit.\n\n- No `all` or `standard` bundle extra: Django has mutually exclusive database\n  backends and platform-restricted extras, making a catch-all extra\n  impractical. Granular extras let users compose exactly what they need.\n  \n#### Notes for mergers\n\nThe `tests/requirements/*.txt` files (`py3.txt`, `postgres.txt`, `mysql.txt`, `oracle.txt`) are\nkept in this PR but marked as **deprecated**. The Jenkins CI infrastructure scripts\n(outside this repository) still reference those files across multiple workflows\n(postgres, mysql, oracle, gis, etc.). Those scripts will need to be updated to\nuse `pip install --group` before those files can be removed. Once Jenkins CI is\nupdated, a follow-up commit can drop them entirely.\n\n#### AI Assistance Disclosure (REQUIRED)\n\n- [ ] **No AI tools were used** in preparing this PR.\n- [x] **If AI tools were used**, I have disclosed which ones, and fully reviewed and verified their output.\n\n> Claude (Sonnet 4.5) was used for code review, documentation, identifying issues, and suggesting\n> fixes during the PyCon US 2026 sprints. All suggestions were reviewed and\n> verified before being applied.\n\n#### Checklist\n- [x] This PR follows the [contribution guidelines](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/internals/contributing/writing-code/submitting-patches/).\n- [x] This PR **does not** disclose a security vulnerability (see [vulnerability reporting](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/stable/internals/security/)).\n- [x] This PR targets the `main` branch.\n- [x] The commit message is written in past tense, mentions the ticket number, and ends with a period (see [guidelines](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/internals/contributing/committing-code/#committing-guidelines)).\n- [x] I have not requested, and will not request, an automated AI review for this PR.\n- [x] I have checked the \"Has patch\" ticket flag in the Trac system.\n- [ ] I have added or updated relevant tests.\n- [x] I have added or updated relevant docs, including release notes if applicable.\n- [ ] I have attached screenshots in both light and dark modes for any UI changes.","created_at":"2026-05-18T22:05:47Z","updated_at":"2026-05-31T00:46:55Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10989528753,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAD-Lgs8AAAACjwbmsQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/labels/PyCon%20%F0%9F%90%8D","name":"PyCon 🐍","color":"4751d6","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/pulls/21312/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.c